    10	//!     σ' = σ + χ·p·I with χ = degree of saturation s (documented). It enters two ways. BUOYANCY:
    11	//!     `project` applies Δv_s = −(Δt/ρ_s)·∇p to the solid velocity field (the SAME ∇p the water
    12	//!     sees; φ_s rides the operator/mass, never the velocity correction — KTD-4), so submerged
    13	//!     grains feel buoyancy through the momentum equation. WET COHESION: the U5 Drucker-Prager
    14	//!     yield apex takes a cohesion arg; U7 wires the saturation→cohesion curve
    15	//!     (`models::cohesion::for_saturation`, Bishop-weighted by χ = s) into it, so a wet bed holds
    16	//!     steeper crater walls than a dry one. The over-packing solids-pressure guard stays INSIDE
    17	//!     the effective/contact partition (never the projection) — the STRESS-PARTITION AUDIT gate
    18	//!     verifies the single-counting.
    19	//!   * SATURATED DEFORMABLE DYNAMICS: the U5 dynamic solid path runs WITH water present and
    20	//!     coupled (drag + buoyancy). Impact momentum arrives through the shared-grid drag/contact
    21	//!     path — NO pairwise impulse bolt-ons (the named failed approach from the prior solver).
    22	//!
    23	//! ============================== CRATER METRIC (pre-committed) ================================
    24	//! The crater is a SIGNED center-vs-rim surface depression measured against the SWELLING
    25	//! baseline: swelling LIFTS the bed, so the crater must be a depression BELOW the swollen
    26	//! surface, not merely the absence of a mound. depth = rim_surface − center_surface, with the
    27	//! surface read from the per-column solid-volume profile (the grain bed top), the rim taken in
    28	//! an annulus clear of the jet, the center taken on the jet axis. FLOOR derivation (below):
    29	//! the floor is set from the jet radius / pour momentum, never calibrated to the solver's own
    30	//! output (a self-calibrated gate cannot fail). vs the documented main/xpbd ≈ 0 baselines.
    31	//!
    32	//! ============================== UNIT / TIME MAPPING (KEEP.md §2) =============================
    33	//! Reused from tests/twofield_infiltration.rs: ≈ 27.7 sim-units/m, τ ≈ 3.685 s_phys/s_sim at
    34	//! |g| = 20. The Terzaghi consolidation gate works in pure reduced units (the T = c_v·t/H²
    35	//! collapse is dimensionless — the two drainage lengths verify the scaling, not an absolute
    36	//! timescale).
    37	//!
    38	//! ============================== KNOB GRID (KTD-9) ============================================
    39	//! U7 adds to the U5/U6/U9 knobs: tf_wet_cohesion (c_max) × tf_cohesion_speak (s_peak) for the
    40	//! effective-stress cohesion; drag_scale (the K-field lever, shared with U6/U9); solid_dynamics
    41	//! (always ON here); the U5 CFL substepping carries over. Exhausting the grid without a pass IS
    42	//! the halt condition (the plan's no-fallback rule) — reported HALT with evidence if the crater
    43	//! floor or any L3 gate can't be met honestly.
    44	
