     5	## Repository Map
     6	
     7	`coffee-sim` is a single Rust + `wgpu` + WGSL crate; the repo root is both the workspace
     8	and the package. Modular blocks under `src/`:
     9	
    10	- `engine/` — orchestration glue: `Scene`, `Simulator`, `State`/`Metrics`, the solver
    11	  `registry`, and the solver-description catalog `engine/solvers.json`.
    12	- `solvers/` — each complete fluid-sim algorithm is a `Solver` (the seam is `base.rs`);
    13	  `noop.rs` are the harness validators. XPBD (primary), MPM, SPH+MPM land here.
    14	- `models/` — shared physics (permeability, extraction, cohesion, wetting, thermal) +
    15	  `Materials`, imported by every solver so cross-solver comparison is fair.
    16	- `emission/` — particle emission (coffee + water), independently testable.
    17	- `profiling/` — local `timestamp-query` + dispatches-per-frame profiler.
    18	- `ui/` — rendering + controls + overlays; consumes only canonical state (one-way data flow).
    19	- `utils/` — shared infra + config: `GpuContext`, spatial hash, SDF, kernels, seeded RNG,
    20	  geometry builders, `Config`, `ParticleBuffers`.
    21	
    22	`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` is authoritative; sub-module plans live in `docs/plans/`. Salvaged
    23	v1 reference values (calibration, units, kernel/SDF math, geometry, target bands) are in
    24	`KEEP.md`. The superseded v1 MPM implementation remains on `origin/*` branches.
    25	
    26	## Working Rules
    27	
    28	- Prefer the smallest correct change over broad refactors.
    29	- Keep physics fixes structural; avoid tuning-only patches for fundamental issues.
    30	- **Never delete or `#[ignore]` tests to go green.** Tests lock conservation/stability/
    31	  plausibility, not temporary heuristics.
    32	- Keep simulation truth out of `ui` — solvers own physical state.
    33	- Stay WASM/WebGPU-portable: keep all device limits at the WebGPU baseline EXCEPT
    34	  `max_storage_buffers_per_shader_stage`, which is raised to 16 (the real per-stage ceiling for our
    35	  targets) — keep bind groups within 16 storage buffers per stage. Flag any native-only feature.
    36	- `todo!()` stubs must compile and be inert — no half-wired pipelines.
    37	
    38	## Verification
    39	
    40	Start with the narrowest relevant check, then before landing a branch:
    41	
    42	- `cargo fmt --check`
    43	- `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`
    44	- `cargo test`
    45	- `cargo run --example phase0_noop`  (headless; skips when no GPU adapter is present)
    46	
    47	## References
    48	
    49	- Start with `README.md`
    50	- Then use `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`

